          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "diretta is the feminine of diretto \"direct\", from Latin dīrēctus \"straight\", the past participle of dīrigere \"to set straight\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
